<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Austrian Lloyd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Österreichischer Lloyd, Lloyd Triestino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Austrian Lloyd was a shipping and insurance company founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trieste">Trieste</a> in 1833, which began steamship services in 1836 and became the largest shipping line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy. Its ships linked Trieste with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and, after the opening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. Transferred to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1919, it continued as Lloyd Triestino.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/austrian-lloyd.jpg" alt="Austrian Lloyd" width="318" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: heied · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erstes_Wappen_%C3%96sterr._Lloyd_1836.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
